=== AUDIT ===
Audited web/src/api/client.ts against the 4 Phase-43 requirements:

  1. Auto-adds /api/v1 prefix exactly once.
     PASS. apiUrl() at L58-66 builds the URL via
       ${getApiBase()}/api/v1${normalizePath(path)}
     -- single concat. resilientFetch fallback (lib/resilience.ts L593)
     likewise prepends exactly once.

  2. Defensive strip when caller passes /api/v1/foo.
     FIX APPLIED. Pre-fix: normalizePath() only ensured a leading slash,
     so /api/v1/foo would concat into /api/v1/api/v1/foo. Post-fix:
     normalizePath() now also runs replace(/^\/api\/v1\//, "/") and
     request() normalises the path ONCE at entry, forwarding the
     canonical form to BOTH directRequest (via apiUrl) AND the
     resilientFetch fallback so neither path can double-prefix.
     Idempotent for the canonical /foo form (no behaviour change for
     the 100% of existing hooks that already conform to engineering
     rule #7).

  3. Preserves snake_case query params.
     PASS. request() does NOT camelCase keys on the request side -- no
     toCamelCase / camelCaseKeys helper appears anywhere on the
     outbound path. The camelCaseKeys transform lives downstream and
     applies only to RESPONSE bodies (handled in lib/resilience.ts /
     consuming hooks).

  4. Surfaces backend errors as ApiError with typed shape.
     PASS. parseError() at L197-210 extracts {message, code} from the
     JSON envelope; directRequest at L230-233 throws
       new ApiError(message, res.status, code)
     so callers can isApiError(err) && err.code === SUDO_REQUIRED_CODE
     / AUTH_MODE_OPEN_CODE without re-parsing.

Hook-side rogue prefix grep (engineering rule #7):
  (none -- verified via grep tool: no hook calls request() with a path
  beginning '/api/v1/'. The only /api/v1 occurrences in api/hooks/ are
  doc comments and an explicit browser-owned download URL builder in
  useExports.ts:163 that does NOT go through request().)

